==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries allows the model to contain a decided application whose EvtSubmitted audit entry is absent, directly violating the append-only invariant. The injection forces exactly such a state to exist.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditTrailComplete, FR_017_NoApplicationDeletion
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_016_AuditTrailComplete: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_017_NoApplicationDeletion: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OnePendingPerCustomer  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OnePendingPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Removing F_OnePendingPerCustomer allows two distinct applications for the same customer to both be in PendingReview simultaneously, violating FR-005. The injection forces this state.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer
      - FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApplication  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApplication.als
    rationale: Removing F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApplication allows two Decision atoms pointing to the same LoanApplication, modelling the concurrent double-decision race that FR-012 and FR-011 prohibit.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_DecidedApplicationImmutable, FR_012_ConcurrencySafety
      - FR_011_DecidedApplicationImmutable: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_ConcurrencySafety: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: Removing F_LeastPrivilege allows an Operation whose caller's role is denied for that OperationKind (e.g., a Customer calling PostDecision). The injection forces exactly such a forbidden operation to exist.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisionAudit, FR_001_CustomerSubmitOnly
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisionAudit: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_001_CustomerSubmitOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditDecisionEntry  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AuditDecisionEntry.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditDecisionEntry allows a decided application to have no decision audit entry at all, breaking the AuditCompleteness and AttributionCorrectness invariants. The injection forces a decided app with no EvtApproved/EvtRejected entry.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_016_AuditTrailComplete, AttributionCorrectness
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditTrailComplete: FAIL (expected)
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccess  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccess.als
    rationale: Removing F_OwnershipBasedAccess allows a Customer-role Operation to target an application owned by a different customer, violating FR-013 and NoInformationLeakage. The injection forces a cross-customer access operation.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_013_CustomerIsolation, NoInformationLeakage
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_CustomerIsolation: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)

